refused: d161_grouping_would_use_colons.cy:7:34, line 7 column 34
 7 |     let $y: f64 = std::math::sin($x);
   |                                  ^^
 what: this is `f64`, where an angle, `f64.std::units::angle.radians`, is needed
 why:  trigonometry asks for an angle in radians, so a plain number is refused, and degrees are converted with `as` (D245)
